PHOTO FROM WIDE WORLD PHOTOS; / The U.S.S. Maryland, classed as the most powerful dreadnaught in the world and carrying eight 16 inch guns, the largest ever mounted on a warship, will soon be ready for the official trial. This is the third of the electric ships her power plant supplying enough electricity to care for all the electric needs in a city of 100,000 population. It has been fitted with practically every electrical appliance used either afloat or ashore. Its big guns will fire a shell of 2,100 pounds for a distance of twenty miles. / 34504 F.C. THE U.S.S. MARYLAND, THE WORLD'S MOST
